{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794244704,"nonce":"790eQH0B3avown0+QhOD8w7aNqA=","title":"jno.precond.form() default inner factors with SuperLU on the real 2n block","message":"With inner=None, _Form.materialize factors the assembled auxiliary once with scipy splu, on the fused real-equivalent block for a complex form. For a 3-D N1E Maxwell twin (curl-curl - k^2 eps mass with first-order faces) at degree 2, this factorisation uses about ten times the peak memory of a complex PARDISO factorisation of the full system at the same mesh. GMRES then needs under a hundred steps, so the preconditioner costs more than solving the system directly.\n\nReproduction: fem.solve(linear=jno.solve.gmres(restart=100), precond=jno.precond.form([curlcurl - k^2 eps mass, local faces])) on a periodic N1E cell; compare the process peak memory with fem.solve(linear=jno.solve.lu(backend='pardiso')).\n\nFix direction: the default inner should factor once with the same direct backend jno.solve.lu() would pick (PARDISO / cuDSS where available, complex-native for a complex form), not SuperLU with its default column ordering on the 2n block.","files":null}]}